    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Eligible studies were full-text original clinical reports enrolling adults with initially unresectable, initially inoperable, or non-upfront-resectable hepatocellular carcinoma who received conversionintent treatment and were subsequently compared according to hepatectomy versus nonhepatectomy management. Eligible reports had to provide extractable comparative time-to-event HRs with 95% CIs for OS, PFS, EFS, DFS, or RFS, provided that the estimate explicitly isolated hepatectomy status.",
      "reason": "The inclusion criteria specify key question elements (adult population with initially unresectable HCC; conversion-intent treatment; comparison hepatectomy vs non-hepatectomy) and a follow-up/estimand requirement (extractable comparative time-to-event HRs for specific survival endpoints with 95% CIs). However, the evidence does not clearly specify eligible study designs, settings, or other question-framework components in a fully comprehensive way."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No retrieved evidence reports eligibility criteria for report characteristics such as dissemination year, language, or publication/report status."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence lists exclusions (e.g., not isolating hepatectomy status, wrong population/type of report), but it does not distinguish exclusion due to outcomes not being measured versus outcomes not being reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "HRs were not entered into synthesis unless the comparison isolated hepatectomy versus nonhepatectomy management.",
      "reason": "The synthesis grouping/comparisons are explicitly defined as those isolating the hepatectomy vs non-hepatectomy management contrast (i.e., only such comparisons were included in synthesis)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Initially unresectable disease was accepted according to the original study definition, protocol designation, or multidisciplinary treatment context [37]. We did not retrospectively impose a uniform technical unresectability definition across heterogeneous published cohorts.",
      "reason": "A rationale is provided for a notable eligibility restriction/approach (not imposing a uniform technical unresectability definition due to heterogeneity across cohorts). However, the evidence does not provide rationales for other notable eligibility restrictions."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 66
}

